      "description": "The cache key uses only record_id, so values are shared across tenants, violating the requirement to cache per (tenant, record_id).",
      "evidence": "Example:\ncache = {}\ndef load(t, r):\n    return f\"{t}:{r}\"\n# First load for tenant 'a'\nprint(candidate.lookup(cache, 'a', '1', load))  # loads 'a:1'\n# Second load with different tenant 'b' but same record_id\nprint(candidate.lookup(cache, 'b', '1', load))  # expected to load 'b:1', but candidate returns 'a:1' because key ignores tenant"
    }
